# 🧸 Raspberry Pi Smart Detector — Animal Alert System

This project uses a Raspberry Pi, YOLOv5 object detection, and OpenCV to distinguish between a bear and a raccoon 
using a 2MP IMX462 Ultra Low Light STARVIS camera. When one of these animals is detected, 
the system plays a corresponding `.mp3` audio alert and logs the detection time and class to a file.

The corresponding mp3 audio alerts are based on the hearing range of the detected preadator.
Each predator class will trigger a mp3 file to be played containing a frequency that is disturbing to their ears,
but unable to be heard by chickens or humans.

## 🎯 Features

- 📷 Real-time image capture using OpenCV and a libcamera-compatible camera
- 🤖 Object detection powered by a custom-trained YOLOv5 model
- 🔊 Plays different sounds when a bear or raccoon is detected
- 📝 Logs detections with timestamps to a text file
- 🧠 Optimized to run on Raspberry Pi 5 hardware
